      "writtenOn": "2020-10-15T19:25:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I do this, it turns out that the device fails to boot due to failure to load the gpio_generic module due to binary incompatibility. I tracked it down to the ifdef in include/linux/gpio/driver.h that enables some struct fields conditional on CONFIG_GPIO_GENERIC. If I remove the ifdef the system boots.\n\nDo you think this would be a reasonable change for upstream? Maybe not since it seems like a GKI-specific binary compatibility issue that they don\u0027t care about. I guess the other thing that we could do is set CONFIG_GPIO_GENERIC\u003dy in gki_defconfig.",
